      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>&lsquo;Cries of grace, grace&rsquo; (Zech 4:7) to the stone of grace, &lsquo;who sits in judgement&rsquo; (Isa 28:6),&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>our master and our teacher Moses the Judge, Bet Din, may he be made fruitful, gifts&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>of wellbeing from me, your friend. Now, I have arrived at &lsquo;a town&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>on the edge of your territory&rsquo; (Num 20:16), wishing you peace and prosperity&nbsp;</li>\n<li>forever, and in great shame and disgrace my times have cast me down&nbsp;</li>\n<li>into the current evil &lsquo;and I cannot flee&rsquo; (Gen 19:19) and a ship</li>\n<li>brought us here against our will. And God has commanded us to hurry</li>\n<li>&lsquo;until the Lord from heaven looks down and sees&rsquo; (Lam 3:50). [&hellip;]</li>\n<li>Yexi&rsquo;el, the least of Israel, son of the scholar Elyaqim&nbsp;</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
